    "chunk_text": "4. Approximately 500 million rupees is\n\nexpected to be spent on research in the field of agricultural mechanization and for promoting new machinery among farming community.\n\n\u2022 Approximately Rs. 100 million is\n\na high yield, it is essential to identify suitable lands and to properly manage and preserve environmental conditions. Accordingly, when identifying suitable lands, factors such as location of land, soil, water source and other environmental factors are taken into consideration. The Department of Agriculture has identified and mapped suitable areas for 12 major crops and seven major fruit crops in Sri Lanka. In addition, a website (https://csrforgnd.doa.gov.lk/) containing information on suitable crops, cultivation seasons and other details at the Grama Niladhari Division level has been developed and maintained so that anyone who requires information could access it. (v) The specific year cannot be mentioned at\n\nthis time. Predicting the specific year in which Sri Lanka will substantially eliminate the importation of major food crops in order to conserve foreign exchange is challenging due to various factors including changes in agricultural policies, climatic conditions, technological advancements and economic developments. Based on medium-term\n\n981 982\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0daf\u0d9a\u0dca.\u0da9\u0dd3. \u0dc1\u0dbd\u0dca \u0d9a\u0dc1\u0dca\u0dad \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dc1]\n\n2026 \u0db8\u0db4\u0dba\u0dd2 05"
