    "md5": "82418a82d0dd84349b9985ea4e8a6ed2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2095,
    "chunk_text": "Through the 1920 short code hotline, it is possible to obtain advice on issues related to coconut cultivation. Relevant information is provided by experienced technical officers in the field.\n\n\u2022 \uf043\uf06f\uf063\uf06f\uf06e\uf075\uf074 Fortnight (\u0daf\u0db4\u0dc1\u0dbd\u0dca \u0daf\u0daf\u0dc3\u0dd2 )\u200d\n\nWith the primary objective of developing coconut cultivation at the grassroots level in closer proximity to growers, the \"Coconut Fortnight (\u0daf\u0db4\u0dc1\u0dbd\u0dca \u0daf\u0daf\u0dc3\u0dd2 ) \u200dProgramme has been implemented as a nationwide mobile initiative, covering all districts. The main objective of this programme is to address the key challenges and issues faced by coconut cultivation and coconut growers through field-level mobile programmes.\n\n\u2022 Establishment of Farmer Leader\n\nUnits - 198 units (2025)\n\nUnder this programme, Farmer Leader Units are planned to be established Island-wide as regional centres to provide services such as facilitating easy access to inputs required by growers and coordinating support from labour force members, when needed. In addition, necessary knowledge is provided to growers through demonstrations covering all coconut cultivation management practices carried out in the field.\n\nDuring that period, the Coconut Cultivation Board has provided the following subsidies to coconut growers:\n\n\u2022 Providing subsidies for planting\n\ncoconut seedlings under proper cultivation.\n\n\u2022 Providing subsidies for infilling\n\n\u2022 Subsidy for providing coconut\n\nseedlings required for home gardening.\n\n\u2022 Providing subsidies for rehabilitation of coconut lands.\n\n\u2022 Water pipe subsidy.\n\n\u2022 Intercropping Subsidy.\n\n\u2022 Subsidy for maintenance of coconut\n\nseedlings planted under proper cultivation.\n\n\u2022 Subsidy for protecting coconut\n\nplantation from wild animals. \u2756 Coconut Development Authority\n\nOver the past 10 years, the Coconut Development Authority has implemented various research and development programmes with the objective of promoting growth in the coconut and coconut-based products sector, identifying consumption trends and formulating extension strategies in line with modern market requirements."
