    "chunk_text": "\u2022 Awareness programmes through\n\nsocial media, electronic media and print media\n\n\u2022 Workshops and training programmes at the regional level\n\n\u2022 Trade exhibitions\n\n\u2022 Consumer awareness promotional campaigns\n\n\u2022 Awareness programmes within\n\n\u2022 Sales promotion programmes -\n\ntargeting both local and international markets\n\n\u2022 B2B Meeting\n\n\u2022 Providing loan facilities to uplift\n\nthe industrialists\n\nThrough these programmes,\n\n\u2022 Increasing public awareness of\n\ncoconut and coconut-based products.\n\n\u2022 Minimizing household coconut\n\nwastage.\n\n\u2022 Increasing the use of packaged\n\ncoconut milk and coconut milk powder products.\n\n\u2022 Expanding domestic market and\n\nincreasing export opportunities.\n\n\u2022 Being able to generate higher\n\nexport income.\n\n\u2022 Improving the ability to identify\n\nconsumption patterns at the regional level and formulate policies.\n\n4. Bank loan facility\n\nA loan scheme called \u201cKapruka\n\nJaya Isura\u201d has been in operation since 2012. These loans are provided to industries for the development of existing industries. This is being implemented in collaboration with financial institutions.\n\nFrom 2015 to 2025, the Regional Development Bank has provided nearly 500 industrialists with approximately Rs. 500 million. The annual interest rate is 6 per cent.\n\n5. Providing subsidies\n\n\u2022 In 2022, under the Livelihood\n\nDevelopment Programme, subsidies were provided\n\n\u2022 To 31 industrialists for drying\n\nmachines,\n\n\u2022 To 17 industrialists for drying\n\nyards.\n\n\u2022 Under the Action Plan, subsidies\n\nwere provided for drying machines\n\n\u2022 To 31 industrialists for the\n\nyear 2021\n\n\u2022 To 11 industrialists for the\n\nyear 2022\n\n\u2022 Under the Action Plan, assistance has been provided for drying yards to 200 entities since 2017.\n\n1027 1028\n\n\u0db4\u0dc1\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dd2\u0daf\u0db8\u0dca\u0dca\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\n\u2022 In 2025, subsidies of Rs. 100,000.00 per person were provided to 23 coconut treacle, coconut jaggery, coconut sugar and coconut ice-cream industries.\n\n\u2022 In 2025, subsidies of Rs. 250,000.00 per person were provided for 18 eco-friendly coconut shell charcoal stoves.\n\n\u2022 Providing assistance for coir"
