    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "95112621eadf4070aa868a1f336cedc6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 723,
    "chunk_text": "It has always been contemplated that a comprehensive legal regime for rescue, rehabilitation and insolvency would be introduced in Sri Lanka. Therefore, even when the Companies Act was being reformed, the insolvency regime was not substantially reformed because even at the\n\ntime, the discussion was to bring in this Bill separately.\n\nThis Bill will repeal the old Insolvency Ordinance, which is completely outdated, as I told you earlier, and amend the Companies Act by repealing provisions relating to liquidation and administration and the Inland Revenue Act by repealing provisions relating to liquidation. Both are Amendments since elaborate provisions relating to liquidation and administration are made in this Bill."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-05-06-2026-05-06",
    "num": "2026-05-06",
    "date_str": "2026-05-06",
    "description": "Hansard of 2026-05-06",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/23536_english_2026-05-06.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-05-06-2026-05-06-0060",
    "chunk_index": 60,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "0af3a601d1f1f59255474c60f720941e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1672,
    "chunk_text": "This Bill will repeal the old Insolvency Ordinance, which is completely outdated, as I told you earlier, and amend the Companies Act by repealing provisions relating to liquidation and administration and the Inland Revenue Act by repealing provisions relating to liquidation. Both are Amendments since elaborate provisions relating to liquidation and administration are made in this Bill.\n\n1073 1074\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dc3\u0da5 \u0dc3\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dc2\u0dba\u0dab \u0db1\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dca\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbb \u0db8\u0dc3\u200d\u0dcf]\n\n2026 \u0db8\u0dd0\u0dba\u0dd2 06\n\nThen, micro, small and medium-sized enterprise - MSME - protection. MSME protection is available to an MSME debtor. An MSME debtor is a company which has a total debt, secured and unsecured, of less than Rs. 50 million. Such a debtor can seek an MSME Company Debt Restructuring Arrangement in terms of Section 278 of the Act; the process is set out in the provisions. An MSME Company Debt Restructuring Arrangement approved by court is binding on all the creditors who are affected by the terms of the Arrangement. An MSME Company Debt Restructuring Arrangement shall be completed when all of the obligations that it created have been discharged. When such Arrangement is completed, under Section 291(4), the debts affected by the Arrangement shall be cancelled and the MSME debtor shall not be liable to pay any part of the debts.\n\nSir, as I mentioned earlier, this is a very comprehensive law and it encompasses almost everything the current law was unable to focus on. Since there is no more time to go into the details of this Bill, I wish, after listening to its overview, the Opposition would support us in making it into a law by passing it today."
  },
