    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "a587bb9b06c08a9b933f0d03e881718c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2100,
    "chunk_text": "Hon. Presiding Member, I would like to deal with this particular piece of legislation - Rescue, Rehabilitation and Insolvency (Corporate and Personal) Bill - that we are discussing today, which has been brought in to amend and consolidate the laws relating to rescue, rehabilitation and insolvency of individuals and companies. This Bill repeals the Insolvency Ordinance, which was enacted way back in the 19th Century, during the colonial period, and also amends the Companies Act, No. 07 of 2007, the Inland Revenue Act, No. 24 of 2017 and the Mediation Boards Act, No. 72 of 1988 and so on and so forth.\n\nIn that regard, I would like to comment on one issue. That is, after cyclone \"Ditwah\", this Government\u2019s colossal failure in trying to assist the aggrieved parties, those who have lost their properties. For instance, I come from the Central Province.\n\n1179 1180\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0ddc\u0db8\u0dca\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dc0\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd6\u0daa \u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0b95\u0bb2\u0b95\u0bae\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b89\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Presiding Member) \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0db8\u0dba\u0dcf, \u0d94\u0db6\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0db8\u0dcf \u0dba\u0dcf\u0dba\u0dd2\u0dba\u200d \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbd\u0dba \u0d85\u0dc0\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dca.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dc3\u0da5 \u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0dc6\u0dca \u0dc3\u0dd3\u0db8\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc3\u200d\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bb0\u0ba3\u0bbf \u0bb0\u0b8a\u0baa\u0bcd \u0bb9\u0b95\u0bc0\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. Rauff Hakeem, Attorney-at-Law) Hon. Presiding Member, I saw that the Bank Supervision Department of the Central Banks has said that only about Rs. 2,000 million had been disbursed by the banks in the Kandy District, whereas Rs. 4,000 million in Badulla District and Rs. 3,000 million in Nuwara Eliya District had been disbursed. But, in the most affected district, the Kandy District, only Rs. 2,000 million had been disbursed. That is because of the reluctance and the risk-averse attitude of the banks and that has to be addressed. I have been looking forward - [Interruption.]- Not only that. - [Interruption.] I know. Now, let me finish because I have limited time."
  },
