    "chunk_text": "A figure of speech that pairs two contradictory or opposite words together to create a paradoxical, often emphatic or humorous effect is called an \"oxymoron\". If you could extend that term \"oxymoron\" to \"oxymoronic behaviour\", I think this Government\u2019s justification of the Emergency is the best-case scenario. Why I say that, Sir, is, in the course of this whole day - I have been here since about lunch time - every single Member from the Government who stood up to speak said that they needed the Emergency to deal with the grave situation caused by Cyclone \"Ditwah\" and now, by the Middle East war. But then, what do they go on to say thereafter in reply to the various shortcomings that were listed by the Members of the Opposition? They rebut the Opposition by saying how brilliantly the Government has dealt with the situation, how so effectively they dealt with the situation. The Hon. Prime Minister, whom I have the utmost respect for, came up with, I think, grades. Everything, she said, was 90 per cent or over 90 per cent! I think there was one which was about 60 per cent, but everything else was over 90 per cent. Then, that is the complete justification for not having the Emergency. You are saying in this House that you have dealt with the situation so well. There is no need for Emergency then.\n\nEmergency, said, \u201cDeclare Emergency.\u201d That is the situation when you must declare Emergency, to deal with a situation that you cannot cope with unless you have the entire system mobilized including the armed forces. But, this is not a situation to declare Emergency. You are falsely trying to justify this and your brief - it is so pathetic - is exposed today and that is the reality."
