    "chunk_index": 54,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "07108db501895b1d245124533c6219db",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1835,
    "chunk_text": "We can also drive cooperation in digital transformation, e-commerce, AI, digital public services education, digital healthcare and digital healthcare renewables and green finance. Our two countries have pledged to work together in harnessing new technologies, including artificial intelligence, e-commerce and digital transformation to foster sustainable development and elevate public service quality. These areas are unfettered by geographical distance. Intellect, technology, innovation and data may well become new bridges to link Viet Nam and Sri Lanka together.\n\nFifth, bolster educational, cultural, tourism and people-to-people connections\n\nViet Nam and Sri Lanka are well-poised to develop cultural, Buddhism, heritage, maritime and eco-tourism. We have reached a common understanding on the importance of air connectivity and encourage air carriers to early open direct flights, while driving measures to facilitate travel, business and people-to-people links.\n\nWe should also enhance the exchange of students, scholars, researchers, artistes and young entrepreneurs; expand scholarship eligibility; advance collaborations between our universities and research institutes and organize Viet Nam cultural weeks in Sri Lanka and vice versa. We treasure your willingness to share with us your experience in archaeology and cultural heritage preservation. We also look forward to bolstering collaboration in the studies of Buddhism, culture and history between us.\n\nI also count on the Parliament, the Government and people of Sri Lanka to continue giving due attention and support to the Vietnamese community in Sri Lanka, for them to lead a stable life, integrate into the local society and make positive contributions to the friendship between our two nations.\n\nSixth, work closely together at regional and international forums"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-05-08-2026-05-08",
    "num": "2026-05-08",
    "date_str": "2026-05-08",
    "description": "Hansard of 2026-05-08",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/23554_english_2026-05-08.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-05-08-2026-05-08-0055",
    "chunk_index": 55,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "d143b75a1413b17241074f626faaf83d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1542,
    "chunk_text": "I also count on the Parliament, the Government and people of Sri Lanka to continue giving due attention and support to the Vietnamese community in Sri Lanka, for them to lead a stable life, integrate into the local society and make positive contributions to the friendship between our two nations.\n\nSixth, work closely together at regional and international forums\n\nOur two countries should continue to work in concert in matters of common concern, such as peace, stability, security and safety of navigation, combating transnational\n\n1441 1442\n\n\u0dcf\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dd2\u0da2\u0dda\u0da7 \u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\ncrime, terrorism, cybercrime and illegal migration; participation in UN peacekeeping, climate adaptation, climate finance for developing countries and the delivery of the Sustainable Development Goals. The 2025 Joint Statement also reaffirmed the importance of peace, stability, security and freedom of navigation and the respect for international law, especially the 1982 UN Convention on the Law of the Sea.\n\nViet Nam welcomes Sri Lanka\u2019s strategy of bolstering cooperation with Southeast Asia and the ASEAN. Viet Nam is ready and willing to be a bridge for Sri Lanka to expand cooperation with the ASEAN, and conversely hope that Sri Lanka would continue to be a bridge between Viet Nam and South Asia and the Indian Ocean.\n\nDear friends, medium and small-sized countries do not seek power through confrontation. We seek power through solidarity, international law, self-reliance, governance quality, the confidence of our peoples and trust among nations."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-05-08-2026-05-08",
    "num": "2026-05-08",
    "date_str": "2026-05-08",
    "description": "Hansard of 2026-05-08",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/23554_english_2026-05-08.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-05-08-2026-05-08-0056",
    "chunk_index": 56,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "583a44d7e0a66fcfdc9dd8f6e71aec21",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1611,
    "chunk_text": "Dear friends, medium and small-sized countries do not seek power through confrontation. We seek power through solidarity, international law, self-reliance, governance quality, the confidence of our peoples and trust among nations.\n\nToday, Viet Nam hopes to translate traditional friendship into an engine for growth in its own right; political trust into concrete economic cooperation; cultural exchanges into profound mutual understanding; shared aspirations into tangible projects, programmes and gains, giving real benefits to our two peoples.\n\nI am confident that the foundation of more than half a decade of diplomatic relations, the commonalities in history, culture and the aspiration to grow, the resolve of our leaders and support of our two peoples will usher in a new developmental period for the relationship between Viet Nam and Sri Lanka, deeper, more substantive and more effective.\n\nHon. Speaker, Hon. Parliamentarians, Dear Friends, from Hanoi to Colombo, from the East Sea to the Indian Ocean, we share the same faith: that peace is the foundation, the people, the centre, development, our target and friendship, the most solid bridge connecting our two nations.\n\nMay the Parliament of Sri Lanka remain a symbol of the will, wisdom and aspiration of the people of Sri Lanka!\n\nMay peace, stability, sustainable development and prosperity be upon the State, the Government and people of Sri Lanka!\n\nMay the bond of friendship and cooperation between Viet Nam and Sri Lanka continue to flourish, in the interest of our two peoples, for peace, stability and prosperity in the region and the world!"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-05-08-2026-05-08",
    "num": "2026-05-08",
    "date_str": "2026-05-08",
    "description": "Hansard of 2026-05-08",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/23554_english_2026-05-08.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-05-08-2026-05-08-0057",
    "chunk_index": 57,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "078fd35f87d040743e2318145fc5b90a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1957,
    "chunk_text": "May peace, stability, sustainable development and prosperity be upon the State, the Government and people of Sri Lanka!\n\nMay the bond of friendship and cooperation between Viet Nam and Sri Lanka continue to flourish, in the interest of our two peoples, for peace, stability and prosperity in the region and the world!\n\nWe appreciate Your Excellency for honouring the invitation extended by the President of Sri Lanka, His Excellency Anura Kumara Dissanayake, during his State Visit to Viet Nam last year to commemorate the 55th Anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between Sri Lanka and Viet Nam and undertaking this State Visit. It is noteworthy that this is your first overseas State Visit to the region following your re-election as President and your re-appointment as the General Secretary of the Communist Party of Viet Nam.\n\nAlthough Sri Lanka-Viet Nam diplomatic relations were established over five decades ago, the historical ties between our people date back many centuries. Sri Lankan Buddhist monks, merchants and travellers fostered early connections with East Asia, including Viet Nam. Those early connections are the foundation of our links today. Over time, this relationship has flourished, grounded in mutual trust and respect and the principle of multilateralism.\n\nOur countries have stood by each other during challenging times. Sri Lanka established diplomatic relations with Viet Nam amidst considerable external pressures, and in turn, Viet Nam has consistently supported Sri Lanka at multilateral fora. The people of Sri Lanka deeply appreciate this solidarity.\n\nThe number of high-level exchanges between our two countries stands as a testament to the strength of our close relationship. Let me recall that President Ho Chi Minh, the founder of modern Viet Nam, visited Sri Lanka on three occasions, reflecting the high value Viet Nam has long placed on its ties with Sri Lanka.\n\n1443 1444\n\n2026 \u0dca\u0dd0\u0dd2\u0db1 08"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-05-08-2026-05-08",
    "num": "2026-05-08",
    "date_str": "2026-05-08",
    "description": "Hansard of 2026-05-08",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/23554_english_2026-05-08.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-05-08-2026-05-08-0058",
    "chunk_index": 58,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "bae479288bbf9bf7a7a3213d7bf7ef9a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1972,
    "chunk_text": "The number of high-level exchanges between our two countries stands as a testament to the strength of our close relationship. Let me recall that President Ho Chi Minh, the founder of modern Viet Nam, visited Sri Lanka on three occasions, reflecting the high value Viet Nam has long placed on its ties with Sri Lanka.\n\n1443 1444\n\n2026 \u0dca\u0dd0\u0dd2\u0db1 08\n\nExcellencies, Hon. Members of Parliament and distinguished Guests, His Excellency T\u00f4 L\u00e2m\u2019s Address to the Parliament of Sri Lanka today is historic, being the first by a Vietnamese leader.\n\nViet Nam\u2019s remarkable progress in recent decades has positioned it as one of the most dynamic and robust economies in our region. This journey is an inspirational example for countries striving towards sustainable and inclusive economic growth and development including Sri Lanka. We have followed with interest your approach to development with its focus on digital transformation, high-quality growth and green development. You have invested in infrastructure upgrading, human capital development and green growth. This is closely aligned to the development trajectory chosen by our Government.\n\nYour Excellency\u2019s extensive experience in public service and leadership, particularly in guiding Viet Nam\u2019s transformation into a regional economic powerhouse and its transition from a purely agricultural economy to an innovative and productivity-driven economic hub is noteworthy. We are pleased that our Hon. Members of Parliament were privileged to hear firsthand about Viet Nam\u2019s development trajectory.\n\nYour Excellency, in your speech today, you mentioned that the people are the root of all things. I think that is a timely and invaluable reminder for all of us, particularly within our Parliament, which is rooted on that principle.\n\nI extend my gratitude to His Excellency T\u00f4 L\u00e2m, President of the Socialist Republic of Viet Nam and General Secretary of the Communist Party of Viet Nam for an inspiring speech."
  },
