    "md5": "7f0fe292ed8eef4ff8d97917504a9ede",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 754,
    "chunk_text": "Your Excellency, in your speech today, you mentioned that the people are the root of all things. I think that is a timely and invaluable reminder for all of us, particularly within our Parliament, which is rooted on that principle.\n\nI extend my gratitude to His Excellency T\u00f4 L\u00e2m, President of the Socialist Republic of Viet Nam and General Secretary of the Communist Party of Viet Nam for an inspiring speech.\n\nIf I may go back in time, it was in 1978 that one of the distinguished leaders of Viet Nam, the then Hon. Prime Minister of Viet Nam, His Excellency Ph\u1ea1m V\u0103n \u0110\u1ed3ng, visited Sri Lanka during the J. R. Jayewardene administration and I remember, distinctly, that, as a small child, I also had the distinguished opportunity of meeting him."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-05-08-2026-05-08",
    "num": "2026-05-08",
    "date_str": "2026-05-08",
    "description": "Hansard of 2026-05-08",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/23554_english_2026-05-08.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-05-08-2026-05-08-0060",
    "chunk_index": 60,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "c24283d3d74fa24e539f321bb83db8b9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2012,
    "chunk_text": "If I may go back in time, it was in 1978 that one of the distinguished leaders of Viet Nam, the then Hon. Prime Minister of Viet Nam, His Excellency Ph\u1ea1m V\u0103n \u0110\u1ed3ng, visited Sri Lanka during the J. R. Jayewardene administration and I remember, distinctly, that, as a small child, I also had the distinguished opportunity of meeting him.\n\nHon. Members of Parliament, Viet Nam is a classic example of economic development, which Sri Lanka must learn from. Both in terms of macroeconomic and microeconomic management, Viet Nam has shown, over the past few decades, how adversity could be overcome and victory attained.\n\nYour Excellency, your visit today symbolizes that both our countries share a common purpose and common religious and cultural traditions. We are inextricably linked by the human values we possess.\n\nMay I also remind you that Viet Nam\u2019s great late Leader Ho Chi Minh visited Sri Lanka not once, not twice, but three times. The great Leader Ho Chi Minh is the epitome of anti-colonialism and anti-imperialism. With few resources, but with great determination, you fought off French colonialism and American imperialism. Today, you are following a model approach - a non-aligned approach, if I may say so - establishing positive alignments with all members of the international community. So, Your Excellency, I congratulate you, your country, your people - the citizenry - and the Government on all your achievements. Also, I would like to take this opportunity to request you to have a closer relationship with Sri Lanka and promote cooperation, specifically in technologically advanced fields such as electronics, artificial intelligence and modern-day technological sectors so that both our countries can move forward and prosper.\n\n1445 1446\n\n\u0dcf\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dd2\u0da2\u0dda\u0da7 \u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\nSurely, Sri Lanka has a lot to learn from your country. We will ensure that your visit acts as a symbol of greater cooperation, establishing mutual respect for each other. Let us move forward as two countries."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
