    "chunk_text": "1. The latest published Gross Official Reserve - GOR - position at the end of April, 2026, which is provisionally estimated, stands at US Dollars 6.8 billion. There is no standard definition for usable reserves. However, the Net International Reserves - NIR - are the difference between Gross Official Reserve - GOR - and the liabilities of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka - CBSL. As per the Central Bank definition, the outstanding international currency swaps and the outstanding IMF-EFF liability of the 2016 Programme are considered as the CBSL liabilities.\n\nSo, compared to 2024, the Net International Reserves increased by US Dollars 1,798 million in 2025, which was an increase of 73 per cent. 2.\n\nYear NIR (USD mn.)\n\n2023 - 404 2024 2,487\n\n2025 4,285\n\nGOR breakdown\n\n(USD mn)\n\nEnd December\n\n2025\n\nEnd March\n\n2026\n\nEnd April 2026(Prov)\n\nOfficial Reserve Assets 6,838 7,026 6,759\n\nForeign Currency Reserve 6,747 6,800 6,505\n\nReserve position in the IMF 4 4 4\n\nSDRs 1 1 32\n\nGold 86 222 219\n\nOther Reserve Assets 0 0 0\n\n1623 1624\n\n2026 \u0db4\u0dd2\u0db6\u0db8\u0db819\u0db8\n\nSo, Special Drawing Rights - SDRs - have increased from US Dollars 1 million in 2025 to US Dollars 32 million in 2026. Then gold reserves, real gold, not paper gold, has increased from US Dollars 86 million in 2025 to US Dollars 219 million in 2026.\n\nAt the end of April, 2026, there was a Bilateral Currency Swap Agreement with the People\u2019s Bank of China. The counterparty was the Central Bank. Principal amount is around US Dollars 1.4 billion and as per the tenure, the Agreement is valid until December, 2027. As regards the maturity profile, it will mature in December, 2027, with the annual roll-over in December, 2026. If we take the all-in cost, at present, there is no cost; the cost is zero as the drawn down CNY Swap."
