    "chunk_text": "At the end of April, 2026, there was a Bilateral Currency Swap Agreement with the People\u2019s Bank of China. The counterparty was the Central Bank. Principal amount is around US Dollars 1.4 billion and as per the tenure, the Agreement is valid until December, 2027. As regards the maturity profile, it will mature in December, 2027, with the annual roll-over in December, 2026. If we take the all-in cost, at present, there is no cost; the cost is zero as the drawn down CNY Swap.\n\nForex swap maturity profile as at 30 April, 2026 with the domestic licensed banks is given below:\n\n3. The Government Gross Official Reserve is immediately deployable except for the proceeds from the People\u2019s Bank of China Swap facility and the forex balance of the Sri Lanka Deposit Insurance Fund.\n\n4. The Central Bank of Sri Lanka does not apply any spread, fee or margin when buying or selling US Dollars from or to the Government of Sri Lanka.\n\nAccordingly, no profit or gain has been realized by the Central Bank of Sri Lanka from US Dollar transactions with the Government of Sri Lanka.\n\n5. The Auditor-General appoints a qualified audit firm to carry out the financial audit of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka - CBSL - in terms of Section 101 of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka Act, No. 16 of 2023. The appointed external audit firm conducts the financial audit and submits its findings to the Auditor-General for the purpose of issuing the audit opinion on the annual financial statements. Based on the report of the external auditor, the Auditor-General issues the audit opinion, which is published together with the annual financial statements in the website of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka and in printed form. The audited financial statements are submitted to the Minister of Finance, Planning and Economic\n\nMaturity Amount (USD mn)\n\n2026 1,814\n\n2027 501\n\n2028 25\n\n2029 3\n\n2,342\n\nDevelopment within four months after the close of the financial year by the Cen