    "chunk_text": "5. The Auditor-General appoints a qualified audit firm to carry out the financial audit of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka - CBSL - in terms of Section 101 of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka Act, No. 16 of 2023. The appointed external audit firm conducts the financial audit and submits its findings to the Auditor-General for the purpose of issuing the audit opinion on the annual financial statements. Based on the report of the external auditor, the Auditor-General issues the audit opinion, which is published together with the annual financial statements in the website of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka and in printed form. The audited financial statements are submitted to the Minister of Finance, Planning and Economic\n\nMaturity Amount (USD mn)\n\n2026 1,814\n\n2027 501\n\n2028 25\n\n2029 3\n\n2,342\n\nDevelopment within four months after the close of the financial year by the Central Bank of Sri Lanka.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dd3 \u0d9a\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bb0\u0bb5\u0bbf \u0b95\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0ba3\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95) (The Hon. Ravi Karunanayake) It is a private auditor?\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 (\u0d86\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dba) \u0d85\u0db1\u0dd2\u0dbd\u0dca \u0da2\u0dba\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 (\u0b95\u0bb2\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf) \u0b85\u0ba9\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0b9c\u0baf\u0ba8\u0bcd\u0ba4) (The Hon. (Dr.) Anil Jayantha) It is not mentioned here.\n\nIn addition, the monthly balance sheets of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka are reviewed by the Auditor-General in accordance with Sri Lanka Standard on Review Engagements - SLSRE - and are published on the Central Bank\u2019s official website. The Auditor-General also makes inquiries from time to time on matters considered necessary in the discharge of his statutory responsibilities and the Central Bank of Sri Lanka provides the required responses and clarifications in a timely manner.\n\n6. In terms of the Section 47(2) of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka Act, No. 16 of 2023, all transactions executed between or among persons resident in Sri Lanka shall be made in Sri Lankan Rupees, unless otherwise authorized by the Central Bank for the purposes of the Foreign Exchange Act, No. 12 of 2017."
