    "chunk_size_bytes": 2036,
    "chunk_text": "6. In terms of the Section 47(2) of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka Act, No. 16 of 2023, all transactions executed between or among persons resident in Sri Lanka shall be made in Sri Lankan Rupees, unless otherwise authorized by the Central Bank for the purposes of the Foreign Exchange Act, No. 12 of 2017.\n\nThe Department of Foreign Exchange has taken several measures during the recent past to prevent transactions effected in foreign currency between persons resident in Sri Lanka. One such measures is the press release dated 12.02.2026 issued by the Central Bank of Sri Lanka with the aim of increasing awareness among the general public and the merchants, explaining applicable legal framework in respect of making payments between persons resident in Sri Lanka in foreign currency, as well as the consequences of engaging in such transactions without obtaining the required approval of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka under the Foreign Exchange Act.\n\n7. The Central Bank of Sri Lanka does not collect such information.\n\n1625 1626\n\n\u0dba\u0daf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dda \u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf\n\n8. As per the Payment Cards and Mobile Payment Systems Regulations No. 1 of 2013 issued under the Payments and Settlements Systems Act, No. 28 of 2005, no person shall engage in the business of or function as a Service Provider except under the authority and in accordance with the terms and conditions of a licence issued by the Central Bank. Those terms and conditions are provided in the Annex and I table* that.\n\nAccordingly, facilitating to accept payments via Payment Cards, that is, functioning as a Financial Acquirer of Payment Cards, in the country requires a licence issued by the Central Bank.\n\nThank you. \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dd3 \u0d9a\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bb0\u0bb5\u0bbf \u0b95\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0ba3\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95) (The Hon. Ravi Karunanayake) \u0dc4\u0db8\u0dbb\u0db4\u0d82\u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dda\u0dc1\u0db8\u0db4\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb \u0dad\u0db1\u0db8\u0d9c\u0db4\u0db1\u0db8\u0dc0 \u0dd2\u0db6\u0db8\u0d94\u0dbb\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8 \u0daf\u0db8\u0dc3\u0dca\u0dc4\u0dc4\u0dca\u0db8\u0dd9\u0dda\u0dc5\u0dad.\u0db8 \u0db8\u0d91\u0dba\u0db8\u0d85\u0d9c\u0dba\u0db8\u0dd9\u0dba\u0db1\u0dcf\u0daf.\u0db8"
