    "chunk_text": "\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014 * \u0dd4\u0dc0\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dad\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbd\u0dc0\u0dda \u0dad\u0db6\u0dcf \u0d87\u0dad. * \u0ba8\u0bc2\u0ba9\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bb2\u0baf\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0b95\u0bb5\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bc1\u0bb3\u0bcd\u0bb3\u0ba4\u0bc1. * Placed in the Library.\n\n\u0dba\u0daf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dda \u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf\n\n(iii)\n\n(vii)\n\nThe measurable outcome is the number of tourist arrivals and the income generated from tourism. They are given in Answer to question number (i).\n\nHowever, despite these promotional efforts, tourist arrivals have also been affected by global factors such as the COVID-19 pandemic, global economic downturns and regional conflicts between countries.\n\n(viii) Short-term Tourism Development Plans\n\nThe Treasury has allocated Rs. 1,000 million for the year 2026 for the implementation of short-term tourism development plans. They are given in Annex 02*.\n\nUnder this, 33 projects at a cost of Rs. 800 million are planned to be implemented, covering all provinces. Among those, 31 projects are scheduled to be implemented, including the restoration of the Dutch Fort in Mannar, the development of the Kammalawella Road in Puttallam, the Blue Flag Beach Project in Pasikudah, the development of the historical sites of Panduwasnuwara and Yapahuwa, the development of the surrounding area of Sembuwatta Lake in Matale and the development of the marine tourism in the Mirissa area.\n\nYear Promotion Expenditure\n\n(Rs.)\n\n2015 786,924,530\n\n2016 844,064,369\n\n2017 1,090,998,703\n\n2018 1,630,389,819\n\n2019 2,331,018,915\n\n2020 489,344,641\n\n2021 380,610,855\n\n2022 666,592,512\n\n1755 1756\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dc0\u0dd2\u0da2\u0dd2\u0dc0\u0db8\u0dda\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dba\u0dca\u0db8 \u0dc4\u0dc0\u0daf]\n\n(iv) There has been no significant changes in the\n\ntop five markets since 2022. (v)\n\n(vi)\n\nYear Average spend per day\n\nAverage length\n\nof stay\n\n2022 USD 164.4 9.34 nights\n\n2023 USD 164.4 8.44 nights\n\n2024 USD 181.15 8.42 nights\n\n2025 USD 148.26 8.29 nights\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014 * \u0dd4\u0dc0\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dad\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbd\u0dc0\u0dda \u0dad\u0db6\u0dcf \u0d87\u0dad. * \u0ba8\u0bc2\u0ba9\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bb2\u0baf\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0b95\u0bb5\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bc1\u0bb3\u0bcd\u0bb3\u0ba4\u0bc1. * Placed in the Library.\n\n2026 \u0db4\u0dd2\u0db6\u0db8\u0db819\u0db8"
