    "chunk_text": "\u201cAllowing depreciation without intervention expands money supply and credit, fueling inflation and thus warranting a tightening cycle for shocks caused by depreciation due to external imbalances and lack of USD cashflows, -\u201d\n\nWhat happened in fuel imports? Within the first three to four months alone, US Dollars 1.2 billion dollars had been spent on that. That is almost two-thirds the cost of fuel imports for the entire last year! So, that is the extent to which this issue has impacted us. Therefore, some serious note has to be taken. India has taken some preventive measures; the Indian Prime Minister has announced a work-from-home programme for people to conserve fuel. Therefore, we also have to take some drastic measures in order to meet this exigency, Sir.\n\nIn the meantime, just a day prior to the imposition of the surcharge on the Customs Import Duty on vehicle imports, some companies had been able to open LCs. How did that happen? That is a serious fraud or a serious corruption involved in this issue. How can somebody open LCs for almost 5,000 vehicles just a day prior to the increase in duties on vehicle imports? So, that is another issue. Earlier, we spoke about sugar imports after there was a reduction of 25 cents in duty, which resulted in Rs. 16 billion being earned by some businessmen. Similar corruption is happening even under this Government. Therefore, that should also be looked into.\n\nHaving said that, I conclude, Sir.\n\nThank you.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dc0\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bc7\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc7\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Speaker) The Hon. Eranga Gunasekara. You have 11 minutes to participate in today\u2019s Debate."
