    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "20e240c3265fb4c72bfb53d759834f4e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1943,
    "chunk_text": "But, the people in the Northern Province, which I represent, Madam, have long-term problems. The Regulations and Resolutions under the Acts we are discussing today are for short-term concerns. If you look at the GDP contribution of the Northern Province, it is at the last place. So, we need fairly serious policies brought into effect, if the Northern Province is to move forward.\n\nThe matter that I wish to raise, Madam, is with regard to education because, at the end of the day, education has\n\nSection 3.3 under Chapter III of the Establishments Code clearly states, I quote:\n\n\"One or more Transfer Boards should be set up in every Department which has twenty five or more transferable officers.\"\n\nAnd, this matter is also referred to in Section 188 of the Northern Provincial Public Service Procedural Regulations Code published in Gazette Extraordinary No. 1817/30 dated 03.07.2013.\n\nFurther, Section 259 of the Gazette Extraordinary No. 2310/29 dated 14.12.2022 states, I quote:\n\n\"Before a public officer is transferred on exigencies of service, the Appointing Authority or the authority with delegated power shall satisfy himself that a need has actually arisen as set out in Section 258 above and that the transfer concerned cannot be deferred till the next annual transfers.\"\n\nThis matter is also referred to in Section 208 of the Northern Provincial Public Service Procedural Regulations Code published under Gazette Extraordinary No. 1817/30 dated 03.07.2013. Furthermore, as specified under the category of \"transfers\" classified under Section 185, these transfers should have been carried out only under the category of \u201cannual transfers.\u201d\n\nMadam, in view of those irregularities in the Northern Province or the way in which they have handled those transfers, many teachers who have already received annual transfers have still not been released from their respective schools by the Northern Provincial education authorities."
  },
