    "chunk_size_bytes": 1965,
    "chunk_text": "That is why we are now in the process of drafting the Cybersecurity Law to establish a Cybersecurity Regulatory Authority to mandate the implementation and reporting of all cybersecurity-related incidents.\n\nThat is why we are introducing this overarching regulatory law to establish the Cybersecurity Regulatory Authority so that all the incidents would be reported to a single entity.\n\n8. The Government of Sri Lanka is expected to implement several urgent coordinated measures to strengthen national resilience against future cyber warfare, cyber threats and organized cybercrime. Those measures include the following, which I will briefly refer to:\n\ni. Mandatory NCSOC onboarding for critical institutions starting with finance, identity, immigration, inland revenue, customs, health, police, transport, social protection and payment-related systems:\n\nii. Enhancement of Threat Hunting and Malware Analysis Capabilities:\n\niii. Priority Implementation of the Information and Cybersecurity Policy:\n\niv. Strengthening Cybersecurity Awareness and Capacity-building:\n\nv. Audit and Compliance Monitoring:\n\nvi. Allocation of Dedicated Cybersecurity Resources:\n\nvii. Strengthening the Legal and Regulatory Framework:\n\nviii. The National Cybersecurity Strategy: (2025-2029)\n\nix. Signing the United Nations Convention against Cybercrime (2025)\n\n2233 2234\n\n[\u0dd9\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d91\u0dbb\u0d82\u0dd9 \u0dd3\u0db8\u0dbb\u0dbb\u0dad\u0dca\u0db1 \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dca\u200d\u0dab]\n\n2026 \u0dd9\u0dd0\u0dba\u0dd2 22\n\nThe Government of Sri Lanka had signed the United Nations Convention against Cybercrime in October, 2025 in Hanoi, reinforcing its commitment to strengthening global cooperation on cybercrime matters. Steps are now being initiated to conduct a comprehensive gap analysis to support the ratification process.\n\nx. Improve other technical measures such as,\n\na. Mandatory Multi-Factor Authentication - MFA - for all government email and privileged accounts, especially finance/ payment workflows.\n\nb. Payment verification protocol for"
