    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/23631_english_2026-05-22.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-05-22-2026-05-22-0085",
    "chunk_index": 85,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "332d4aea04c48abf59f4541fe5d1f12b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1604,
    "chunk_text": "The Lanka Sama Samaja Party has had such a long history in this House. Though the left politics has seen many ups and downs, the Hon. (Prof.) Vitarana remained very forthright and committed to the ideals of his party\n\nand his anti-imperial attitude in this House would always be remembered. He took that fight even in the Cabinet against many policy decisions which seemed to favour the capitalist class.\n\nMore than anything else, I would remember him as someone who stood for devolution of power for minorities. His served as the Chairman of the All Party Representative Committee, which was set up by the then President Mahinda Rajapaksa to resolve the ethnic conflict, and to date, its Report is considered one of the best reports that had been submitted on resolving the ethnic crisis. That report is referred to as the \u201cTissa Vitarana Report\u201d. His contribution to the deliberations of that Committee, to which my party, too, was a party, and several other All Party Conferences and Select Committees in Parliament would be very fondly remembered.\n\nAlso, being a medical professional and a scientist, his contribution had been unparalleled. He pioneered the establishment of the SLINTEC in the nanotechnology sector of this country while he was the Minister of Science and Technology.\n\nHe also made an immense contribution to the scientific sector in the country. At one time, he was the Director of the Medical Research Institute and being there, he looked into epidemics such as cholera and various other epidemics and had been involved in serious research, contributing immensely in that area."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-05-22-2026-05-22",
    "num": "2026-05-22",
