    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "ba6e22761d66c159c0063b9346efb4f8",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1770,
    "chunk_text": "He also made an immense contribution to the scientific sector in the country. At one time, he was the Director of the Medical Research Institute and being there, he looked into epidemics such as cholera and various other epidemics and had been involved in serious research, contributing immensely in that area.\n\nThen, I will move on to the next Hon. Member. The late Hon. Chandradasa Galappaththi was a Member who came to this House when I entered Parliament way back in 1994, almost 32 years ago. We came to this House as freshers and since then, we had been friends.\n\n2247 2248\n\n\u0db4\u0dab\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dae\u0dd2\u0dc3 \u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dc0\n\nHaving originally worked in the Gal Oya Project, which was initiated by the late Hon. D. S. Senanayake, he got into politics. He entered local government politics and became the first Chairman of the Ampara Urban Council. Thereafter, he contributed towards making the United National Party win the Ampara Electorate, which was unable to be won ever since it was created in 1960 upto 1977 as it was the bastion of the Sri Lanka Freedom Party. But, it was the late Hon. Chandradasa Galappaththi and the late Hon. P. Dayaratne who pioneered in making the United National Party win the Ampara Electorate. Since then, he had been a member continuously for several years, perhaps for 15 to 20 years, representing the Ampara District and I had the privilege of being elected for the Ampara District once, where he was my co-candidate. Then, he also served the provincial council system and we had the pleasure of having him as the Chairman of the Eastern Provincial Council while the member from my party was the Chief Minister. He had served the Ampara District with such a faithful dedication and I would convey my condolences to his wife and children."
  },
