    "chunk_text": "Now, Sir, I would like to pay my respects and express condolences on the death of the Hon. (Prof.) Tissa Vitarana. I happened to be a Member of Parliament when he was also a Member of Parliament during my first stint from 2001 to 2010.\n\nMadam, for me, the key moment which made me respect him more - it might not be a very important event in the larger scheme of things - was this. I have known of him because of his interest in wanting to find a solution to the ethnic conflict, being a moderate amongst the Sinhala leaders who always tried to find common ground with the Tamil People. So, all of those qualities are things that we, as Tamil nationalists who have been trying hard in our own way to find a solution to our national question, would respect. But, the one incident that, I think, made him stand out was when - he was a very senior Minister during Gotabaya Rajapaksa\u2019s time and when the COVID-19 struck - because of his professional expertise, he did not agree with the Government\u2019s position at that time with regard to cremating COVID-infected bodies, especially Muslim janazahs. He was\n\n2277 2278\n\n[\u0dd9\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dc0\u0db1.\u0dc0\u0db1. \u0dc3\u0db4\u0dab\u0db1\u0dca\u0db1 \u0db6\u0dbd \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dca\u200d\u0dab]\n\n2026 \u0dd9\u0dd0\u0dba\u0dd2 22\n\nsomeone who was very critical of that policy. At a time when Gotabaya Rajapaksa had made a resounding victory and when everyone, whether it be Government Members or even some Members in the Opposition, did not want to cross his path, the Hon. (Prof.) Vitarana was a man who was willing to stand up for what he believed in was something wrong that the Government was doing. I thought that was a quality that had the potential to do a lot of good, and true to those qualities of his and in that light, he would always be respected.\n\nMadam, I would like to pay my respects to his family, his party and to all his supporters today.\n\nThank you. \u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dab \u0db1\u0dd2\u0db4\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0dca\u200d\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0d9a \u0dc4\u0db7\u0dcf \u0dc4\u0db7\u0dcf\u0db4\u0dd2 \u0dd4\u0dbb\u0db8\u0dd2\u0dba (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b95\u0bc1\u0bb4\u0bc1\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bcd \u0ba4\u0bb5\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bbe\u0bb3\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Chairperson of Committees) \u0dd9\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d86\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dae.\u0d91 . \u0dbb\u0d82\u0da2\u0dd2\u0dad\u0dca \u0dd9\u0daf\u0dca\u0dc0,\u0dd9 \u0db6\u0dab\u0dca\u0da9\u0dab\u0dbb \u0dd9\u0db1\u0dca\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dd9\u0dab."
  },
